The new command builds and mostly mirrors the prior implementation, but its primary tracked-AIG diagnostic can report a valid-looking node ID when the tracked AIG is absent. That makes the diagnostic output misleading for the scenario this iteration is meant to study.

Review comment:

- [P2] Use an absent sentinel for tracked nodes — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/abcStmap_59.c:81-81
  When the tracked AIG never gets inserted into the pressure table, `memset` leaves `TrackedNode` as `0`, so the diagnostics report `tracked-node = 0` even though no mapped node was found. This happens in the current stmap59 runs with zero tracked ratios, and it undermines the new diagnostic's ability to distinguish an absent AIG from a real node; initialize `TrackedNode` to `-1` after clearing.
